// A local development workspace. Copy it OUTSIDE this repo — to the directory
// that CONTAINS gohort and its sibling modules — and fix the paths:
//
//	.../github.com/cmcoffee/
//	├── go.work        <- here, not inside gohort
//	├── gohort/
//	└── snugforge/
//
// You need this ONLY if you develop gohort alongside a local checkout of one of
// its dependencies. Building a release from a clean clone does not need it:
// go.mod resolves published modules by itself, which is the entire reason the
// overrides are not in go.mod any more.
//
// What it buys: edit snugforge, and gohort picks the change up on the next
// build. No tag, no version bump, nothing to remember to undo before pushing.
//
// TWO PATH RULES, both learned the hard way on a tree reachable through a
// symlink (/home/craig/workshop/cmcoffee -> /mnt/workshop/go/src/...):
//
//   - `use` paths RELATIVE. Go has to match your current directory against one
//     of them textually; an absolute path stops the workspace applying when you
//     cd in through the other name.
//   - `replace` targets ABSOLUTE whenever they climb above the workspace
//     directory. A relative "../go-pdf/fpdf" resolves to a different place
//     depending on which name you came in through — one of them nonexistent.
//
// A module with no go.mod cannot join a workspace (kitebroker, for one). It
// keeps building the old way, untouched.

go 1.25.0

use (
	./gohort
	./snugforge
)

replace (
	// Third-party copies patched locally: overrides, not modules under
	// development, so they are replaced rather than `use`d.
	github.com/go-pdf/fpdf      => /abs/path/to/go-pdf/fpdf
	github.com/rwcarlsen/goexif => /abs/path/to/rwcarlsen/goexif

	// Only needed while snugforge is untagged. `use` above supplies its source,
	// but gohort's go.mod requires v0.0.0 — a placeholder that exists nowhere —
	// and the module graph still has to resolve that version. Pinned to v0.0.0
	// rather than all versions, which Go refuses alongside `use`.
	//
	// Delete this the day snugforge is tagged and the requirement is bumped.
	github.com/cmcoffee/snugforge v0.0.0 => /abs/path/to/cmcoffee/snugforge
)
